-- title:
--   Continuity of the Generated Semigroup Orbit
-- statement:
--   This is the continuity statement for the orbit generated by a closed densely defined operator.
--
--   Let $H_0,H_1$ be complete real Hilbert spaces, let $T:H_0\to H_1$ be a linear partial map, let `hT` assert that $T$ is closed, and let `hd` assert that its domain is dense in $H_0$. For every $f\in H_0$, the generated orbit $t\mapsto P_t f$, represented by `Generated.apply T hT hd t f`, is continuous on the nonnegative half-line:
--
--   $$t\mapsto P_t f\quad\text{is continuous on }[0,\infty).$$
--
--   This is a semigroup regularity statement for nonnegative times.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Analysis/Semigroup/Generated/Laws.lean#L396-L426 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Analysis.Semigroup.Generated.Laws`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Analysis.Semigroup.Generated.continuousOn`; the repository is private at upload time).

